{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity","id":1475168,"title":"Why don't more vampires follow the path of harmony instead of humanity?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-21T19:12:01-08:00","id":1475168,"title":"Why don't more vampires follow the path of harmony instead of humanity?","content":"Now I know what some of you are going to say, &quot;VTM is about struggling with keeping your humanity!&quot;. And I agree with that statement, its just that if you stop thinking of vtm as a game and as a real world, your opinion would change. Humanity is perhaps one of the most limiting morality system within the the vtm world. I say this because as a vampire you are going to have to break a lot of its rules nightly. There was someone on reddit who posted why humanity was such a terrible path to follow and explained it great. This was kind of inspired by them. <br /> <br /> Feel free to read their post here= <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/vtm/comments/pr3a7s/if_killing_10_mortals_is_more_or_less_all_it/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.reddit.com/r/vtm/comment...r_less_all_it/</a> <br /> <br /> (You may have to copy and paste it in another tab for it to open)<br /> <br /> I don't think I really need to explain anything about the path of harmony, since the wiki already explains the gist of it. The link of which I will post below.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Humanity_(VTM\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Humanity_(VTM</a>)<br /> <br /> My question to all of you is why don't more vampires follow the path of Harmony?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T19:28:15-08:00","id":1475171,"title":"","content":"The Path of Harmony is actually really hard to follow. It's almost a monk's path. You can't act bestial towards humans, but you can't get too close to them either. Which, in practice, leads to this very cold ascetic existence, where you're generally very polite to humans and don't disrupt their lives, but periodically end them for the sake of food and secrecy. It's a difficult and lonely path to follow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T19:43:20-08:00","id":1475173,"title":"","content":"The path has always felt like something of a cop out, that is a way to avoid some of the narrative conflicts the game is design to embrace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T19:50:58-08:00","id":1475175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity#post1475168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I agree with that statement, its just that if you stop thinking of vtm as a game and as a real world, your opinion would change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would I think of VtM as a real world? It's a game world. It only needs to withstand suspension of disbelief.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Humanity is perhaps one of the most limiting morality system within the the vtm world. </div> </div> </div>It really isn't, especially when you consider what simply having Instinct instead of Self-Control means for your character.<br /> <br /> People complain about the Paths being &quot;the Path of what I was going to do anyway,&quot; but that can be Humanity too. Humanity only seems limiting because it's the baseline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I say this because as a vampire you are going to have to break a lot of its rules nightly. </div> </div> </div>Such as?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There was someone on reddit who posted why humanity was such a terrible path to follow and explained it great. This was kind of inspired by them. </div> </div> </div>The poster there is treating the mathematical abstractions of the game as the game's &quot;physics&quot; rather than mechanics for highlighting specific moments in a vampire's life. A vampire has zero chance of botching or Frenzying feeding 99.9999999999% of the time because <b>you don't roll</b> for all those times. The rules themselves say that. The whole attempt to &quot;prove Humanity bad&quot; with math doesn't follow the rules of the game, so it's inherently faulty.<br /> <br /> There's also a huge amount of &quot;bad STs can screw you if you're on Humanity,&quot; without any recognition that can be done with any Path.<br /> <br /> Just look at Harmony. Vandalism is a level 1 sin for Harmony. Surprising someone such that they drop and break something value ten times could turn you into a Wight. The idea that Humanity is uniquely fragile doesn't hold up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My question to all of you is why don't more vampires follow the path of Harmony? </div> </div> </div>1) Harmony is a shitty Path for most people.<br /> 2) You start on Humanity and changing to a different Path is difficult. Lots of vampires lose themselves to the Beast trying.<br /> 3) Instinct is a horrible Virtue for most vampires.<br /> etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T20:05:52-08:00","id":1475176,"title":"","content":"Anyone who thinks the Path of Harmony is easy hasn't read it. It is an incredibly ascetic path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T20:29:55-08:00","id":1475177,"title":"","content":"I've always assumed that the jettisoning of the Path of Harmony with the launch of Revised Edition had something to do with the fact that it's a horrifyingly racist spin on &quot;The Path of What I Was Going To Do Anyways.&quot; <br /> <br /> Don't feel guilty for killing humans, but also protect the environment! And it's attributed to the Sabbat's adoption of &quot;Native American beliefs.&quot; <br /> <br /> This is a prime example of the kind of nonsense Second Edition is infamous for. Nothing of value was lost when the Sabbat canonically purged its followers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T20:31:57-08:00","id":1475178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity#post1475168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I know what some of you are going to say, &quot;VTM is about struggling with keeping your humanity!&quot;. And I agree with that statement, its just that if you stop thinking of vtm as a game and as a real world, your opinion would change. Humanity is perhaps one of the most limiting morality system within the the vtm world. I say this because as a vampire you are going to have to break a lot of its rules nightly. There was someone on reddit who posted why humanity was such a terrible path to follow and explained it great. This was kind of inspired by them.<br /> <br /> Feel free to read their post here= <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/vtm/comments/pr3a7s/if_killing_10_mortals_is_more_or_less_all_it/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.reddit.com/r/vtm/comment...r_less_all_it/</a><br /> <br /> (You may have to copy and paste it in another tab for it to open)<br /> <br /> I don't think I really need to explain anything about the path of harmony, since the wiki already explains the gist of it. The link of which I will post below.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Humanity_(VTM\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Humanity_(VTM</a>)<br /> <br /> My question to all of you is why don't more vampires follow the path of Harmony?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the reason the Path of Harmony was not more wildly followed is because it is really hard to be partially a monster. You can either be someone who knows what is right and fail to achieve it (Humanity) or you can go whole hog to be a monster (Low Humanity, Other Paths). Its hard to say, &quot;It's okay to eat humans but only because you're hungry and not to be mean to them in any other way.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475177#post1475177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always assumed that the jettisoning of the Path of Harmony with the launch of Revised Edition had something to do with the fact that it's a horrifyingly racist spin on &quot;The Path of What I Was Going To Do Anyways.&quot; Don't feel guilty for killing humans, but also protect the environment! And it's attributed to the Sabbat's adoption of &quot;Native American beliefs.&quot; This is a prime example of the kind of nonsense Second Edition is infamous for. Nothing of value was lost when the Sabbat canonically purged its followers.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are both 100% correct but because they revised the Path of Harmony into the Path of the Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-21-2022, 11:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T21:40:03-08:00","id":1475183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475177#post1475177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always assumed that the jettisoning of the Path of Harmony with the launch of Revised Edition had something to do with the fact that it's a horrifyingly racist spin on &quot;The Path of What I Was Going To Do Anyways.&quot;<br /> <br /> Don't feel guilty for killing humans, but also protect the environment! And it's attributed to the Sabbat's adoption of &quot;Native American beliefs.&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a poorly thought out Path. But second edition at least had the excuse it was infodumping a lot of stuff and couldn't afford to detail everything as much as we'd like. Based on the information provided in the original Sabbat Guides, I thought there was a significant faction of Sabbat that were vampires of early Native Americans embraced by Country Gangrel early in colonial history. They reconciled their beliefs they had when they were mortals with their new existence. This is based on stuff written for the Path of Harmony, Gangrel anti-tribu, mentiosn of the Penumbra of Gray Squirrels, and a few other places. They represented a distinct faction of the Sabbat, primarily nomad packs (or at the very least not urban based) that were in the Sabbat as default simply because that is how their sires were. But they weren't very interested in the sect. Likely aligned with the Loyalist movement as that did not impose any restrictions to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475177#post1475177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a prime example of the kind of nonsense Second Edition is infamous for..</div> </div> </div> </div>The Path itself was poorly written, but so were all the other pacts. It needed to be updated as well. Second Edition could be very gonzo at times, and that's not to everyone's tastes. (It's not mine either.) But it provided a lot of tools for STs to do what they wanted in the setting which was a good thing. It was just up to STs to prune away the branches they didn't want and make adjustments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475177#post1475177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing of value was lost when the Sabbat canonically purged its followers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, but understand your point of view. If all it is was a path for white guys who watched Dances with Wolves, it was a shitty aspect and nothing was missed by its absence. But I feel the Path of Harmony had two things that made it interesting. First that it was primarily made up of vampires who were Native Americans and represented a unique take on people adapting to their vampire status. That alone made it an interesting faction within the Sabbat. The second was that as one of the more humane Paths, it was an interesting &quot;heresy&quot; within the Sabbat that showed the sect was more than just doing evil (which was important as well).<br /> <br /> Neither aspect was important to the metaplot railroad that said the only narrative use an ST could have for the Sabbat was as a paramilitary sect to kill Camarilla vampires and make the game solely about sect wars right before Gehenna. I think that metaplot was a huge mistake because STs could have lots of other uses of the Sabbat in their chronicles, and taking away those tools to do something different disempowered STs. It said that what they were doing was wrong.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T21:44:42-08:00","id":1475184,"title":"","content":"I took an entirely different tact on the Path of Harmony and assumed it was the Sabbat purging all of its members that didn't engage in overt horrific evil for the sake of being evil. It was not the Native American element, which I think was something I'd honestly forgotten since it was practically irrelevant, but the fact it was against the Achilli-designed Revised take on the Sabbat where they went from being:<br /> <br /> &quot;Why should we care about mortals? We're above mortals and something else entirely.&quot;<br /> <br /> To<br /> <br /> &quot;BURN, TORTURE, PILLAGE! WE'RE EVIL MAN!&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T23:24:25-08:00","id":1475195,"title":"","content":"The real conundrum is why don't all vampires follow Kings/Chivalry/Vizier/Honourable accord because these are obviously the best roads for undead society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T23:57:06-08:00","id":1475199,"title":"","content":"The in game, because people already talked the raw and meta reasons, reason basically boils down to one fact: you start human. Only humans can easily become vampires, which means humanity is the natural path to start with. In the modern night, almost no path exists outside the independents or Sabbat, so humanity is all you got.<br /> <br /> Btw, paths are corruptions of the old roads. Old roads could be as similar, or completely alien, to humanity as they get. This ironically is best represented in the ability to appear alive, something the modern paths lack. During the formation of the Camarilla and Sabbat, the Sabbat began to take the old roads and twist their philosophies and ideals to fit with their political agenda. This is why in every edition of vtm, paths are a Sabbat thing. This made to where only paths couldn't pass for the living with ease, and so the Camarilla began to discourage Paths completely, or more actually prevent the newly embraced from hear about paths at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":26764,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","user":"Vilenecromancer","date":". 02-22-2022, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T00:01:22-08:00","id":1475201,"title":"","content":"Btw what counts as a violation, can make humanity so much easier, or harder, to maintain then a path. For some example, some people will view not following a religious tradition is worth a violation, but others would shrug. Even in v20, humanity is the most customizable moralities in the game. Sadly morality is poorly explained in all editions, and there's no way for me to explain it in a way that makes sense really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T06:24:53-08:00","id":1475231,"title":"","content":"I feel this path would make a lot of sense if you're a Gangrel. Plus as long as you keep to your self most of the time you should be fine. The path states that you can interact with mortals to stave of boredom, but you have to remember you're not one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 02-23-2022, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T09:36:00-08:00","id":1475238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475231#post1475231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel this path would make a lot of sense if you're a Gangrel. Plus as long as you keep to your self most of the time you should be fine. The path states that you can interact with mortals to stave of boredom, but you have to remember you're not one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That plus a specific bloodline where the one's who practiced it in the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T10:05:12-08:00","id":1475240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475195#post1475195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The real conundrum is why don't all vampires follow Kings/Chivalry/Vizier/Honourable accord because these are obviously the best roads for undead society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honor is for suckers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T10:19:58-08:00","id":1475243,"title":"","content":"I think a way to rephrase that is that it would behoove the Camarilla to encourage their own version of Honorable Accord/etc. among the younger vampires because it would help maintain order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T11:17:45-08:00","id":1475246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475243#post1475243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a way to rephrase that is that it would behoove the Camarilla to encourage their own version of Honorable Accord/etc. among the younger vampires because it would help maintain order.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would also be a lot of work. Keep in mind, you're not just teaching someone honor, you're pounding it into them so hard that it replaces humanity. Elders can actually be pretty lazy, especially on subjects that don't require a ton of effort.<br /> Let's say you've got a Nosferatu Elder, and he was an architect in life and continues to be one in undeath. He's got a rivalry with a Toreador elder who is also an architect. The Nos creates these oddly beautiful homes in rustic-industrial style, and the Toreador creates more conventionally beautiful homes. These two have been frenemies for a long time and spend a lot of time trying to woo clients from each other. They also have touchstone relationships they try to maintain. They also like really good blood and try to keep their relationships with the circulatory system friendly. They also both need to kiss up to the Prince periodically. They also just want to sit back and read a book or take in a movie occasionally.<br /> <br /> These guys don't have a ton of time left after doing all that. They don't want to spend it all pounding honor into a neonate who might end up a wight because of it. Mostly they just want those neonates to do their jobs without breaking the masquerade. You're an accountant? Good, you're a vampire now, handle my finances, and don't break the masquerade, other than that I don't give a damn what philosophy you hold to.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T12:15:40-08:00","id":1475249,"title":"","content":"It's work, but work the Sabbat regularly manages. So I'm pretty sure the Camarilla could have the necessary infrastructure to guide vampires bad at Humanity onto approved Paths.<br /> <br /> Esp. if you're running an altered version of the setting that better incorporates later additions like Roads into the history of the Camarilla and the Road of Kings and the Road of Heaven always had some presence in the Cam leading to modern Cam friendly versions of Paths.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T13:16:16-08:00","id":1475251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475243#post1475243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a way to rephrase that is that it would behoove the Camarilla to encourage their own version of Honorable Accord/etc. among the younger vampires because it would help maintain order.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Camarilla also encourages obedience and blind loyalty but we know how well that works.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T13:29:40-08:00","id":1475253,"title":"","content":"Wasn\u2019t the Path of Harmony wiped out like a long time ago?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T14:02:38-08:00","id":1475254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475251#post1475251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Camarilla also encourages obedience and blind loyalty but we know how well that works.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would work a lot better with more neonates/ancillae on Honorable Accord than it does with them just having low Humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475253#post1475253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn\u2019t the Path of Harmony wiped out like a long time ago?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. It's only existed for ~300 years in the first place. It was purged from the Sabbat, but relatively recently, and continues to exist largely among Gangrel in Cam (not always loyal to it) areas as it's tolerated by some Cam princes due to it's emphasis on not being disruptive.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T14:18:38-08:00","id":1475255,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't the Path of harmony actually be well liked within the camarilla, I can see a lot of elders being happy about having vampires in their cities follow a path that teaches them not vandalize or disrupt the world around them? Plus at higher levels there's a rule against playing the jyhad.<br /> <br /> Sure it would be somewhat difficult to follow, but that's the same for humanity and the other paths. This one seems like the one that guarantees you a chance of surviving for a couple hundred years. Of course accidents happen.<br /> <br /> I can actually see a lot of vampires being attracted to this path. It pretty much gives you the guidelines on how to coexist with humanity as a vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T14:39:33-08:00","id":1475256,"title":"","content":"The two biggest problems are Instinct (I know I harp on this a lot, but not being able to stop a Frenzy at all is a huge problem for the Cam even if high Instinct gives you much better control over Frenzies), and that Harmonists have to resist others making changes to the world at level 5. Having a bunch of Harmonists around when you want to rezone an area to build a new rack is a pain in the ass the higher ups in the Cam don't need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T15:19:58-08:00","id":1475259,"title":"","content":"Setting aside that Elders don't want to too overtly preach an ethical code they don't practice (being too honorable would get in the way of their plotting), Camarilla vampires wouldn't necessarily mandate Honorable Accord because of the risk of their childer going into Wassail.<br /> <br /> Sabbat vampires tend to not care if their progeny become wights. Reclaim the blood or throw them at a Camarilla city, then Embrace another. Heck, Embrace a whole group. Some of them will survive the transition to a Path with most of their capacity for rational thought intact. It's chucking them against the wall to see what sticks.<br /> <br /> Camarilla vampires, by contrast, tend to be much more protective of their offspring. If for no other reason than because they need special permission to Embrace in the first place. So anything that might jeopardize that childe is a risk that must be assessed carefully. For most Kindred, there's just not enough incentive to force a Path transfer, if your primary motivation is to keep the Masquerade and have your childer be loyal.<br /> <br /> There are way easier ways to keep a Fledgling under your thumb, and to make them keep their existence secret. Ones that don't require a harrowing spiritual journey with no guarantee of &quot;survival&quot;.<br /> <br /> Humanity, though an imperfect instrument for the vampiric unlifestyle, suits the Camarilla's purposes well enough. And it's the default state for vampires, which makes it easy. And if there's anything that vampires like better than blood or crushing their enemies, it's doing the easy thing. It's why so many Kindred Elders hover around Humanity 4 (from all the moral compromises they do for expedience).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T15:46:42-08:00","id":1475261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475254#post1475254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would work a lot better with more neonates/ancillae on Honorable Accord than it does with them just having low Humanity.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If you somehow brainwashed them all, I suppose so, yes. But if you can't get them to want to obey you and the law, I'm not sure how you can get them to completely upend their personal morality to become someone who literally has a worldview entirely devoted around fanatical loyalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T15:54:28-08:00","id":1475262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475256#post1475256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The two biggest problems are Instinct (I know I harp on this a lot, but not being able to stop a Frenzy at all is a huge problem for the Cam even if high Instinct gives you much better control over Frenzies), and that Harmonists have to resist others making changes to the world at level 5. Having a bunch of Harmonists around when you want to rezone an area to build a new rack is a pain in the ass the higher ups in the Cam don't need.</div> </div> </div> </div>But wouldn't harmony level 6 stop most from trying to interfere, since it may be a stronger vampires domain?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T16:09:44-08:00","id":1475264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475259#post1475259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Setting aside that Elders don't want to too overtly preach an ethical code they don't practice (being too honorable would get in the way of their plotting), Camarilla vampires wouldn't necessarily mandate Honorable Accord because of the risk of their childer going into Wassail.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who said anything about mandate it? The idea is to remove the Camarilla intolerance of it, and even have the Cam use it as a tool by encouraging some Kindred to take it up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475261#post1475261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you can't get them to want to obey you and the law, I'm not sure how you can get them to completely upend their personal morality to become someone who literally has a worldview entirely devoted around fanatical loyalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>You make it special. It's something off-limits but for the chosen. You dangle it as a perk that lets you do things other Cam vampires can't do. You make sure there's a prominent Archon or even a Justicar on it that got there because of it. You make it seem like a different way to get ahead in the Cam without playing the normal Cam games.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475262#post1475262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But wouldn't harmony level 6 stop most from trying to interfere, since it may be a stronger vampires domain?</div> </div> </div> </div>That just means you have to pick which sin you want to roll for.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T16:58:18-08:00","id":1475272,"title":"","content":"Amusingly, I fully buy the Path of Honorable Accord falling out of favor with the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Why?<br /> <br /> Because in any ideology-driven organization, there's eventually a purge of the true believers. See Stalin and the Bolsheviks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T19:12:42-08:00","id":1475281,"title":"","content":"Honorable Accord is definitely the &quot;break glass in case the Sabbat's Elders need disposable troops&quot; path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T20:26:56-08:00","id":1475285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475254#post1475254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would work a lot better with more neonates/ancillae on Honorable Accord than it does with them just having low Humanity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not really. It's only existed for ~300 years in the first place. It was purged from the Sabbat, but relatively recently, and continues to exist largely among Gangrel in Cam (not always loyal to it) areas as it's tolerated by some Cam princes due to it's emphasis on not being disruptive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T20:34:01-08:00","id":1475287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475272#post1475272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Amusingly, I fully buy the Path of Honorable Accord falling out of favor with the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Why?<br /> <br /> Because in any ideology-driven organization, there's eventually a purge of the true believers. See Stalin and the Bolsheviks.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Or Hitler\u2019s Night of Long Knives when they purged the Brownshirts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T02:47:06-08:00","id":1475304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Players Guide to the Sabbat, page 95</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Path of Harmony developed in the late 1700s in the New World colonies. The Path enjoyed a great deal of growth in its early years, but its numbers have begun to dwindle because of the renewal of constant Jyhad. Most of the Sabbat have become too jaded to accept the ways of this Path. The Path of Harmony synthesized the various <b>philosophies of the Romantics,</b> including <b>American ideals</b> and <b>transcendentalism.</b> It put as much emphasis on <b>emotion and divine Providence</b> as it did on the <b>natural law established by God.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Not that anyone here will care, I suppose, but the above excerpt is what the actual Second Edition text says about the history and development of the Path of Harmony (emphases mine, of course). &quot;Native American beliefs&quot; are not mentioned even once in the writeup, nor are Harmonists identified with Native Americans anywhere in <i>The Players Guide to the Sabbat.</i><br /> <br /> The entire Path of Harmony = Native Americans thing seems to be a product of the Revised Edition version of the Path of Harmony in the <i>Sins of the Blood</i> supplement (pages 35-37). The Revised version is also responsible for the Path's &quot;protect the environment&quot; angle that is absent from the original.<br /> <br /> This has to be one of the most hilarious self-owns by Revised proponents I have ever seen on these forums. Should we qualify the assertions earlier in this thread by stating instead that this horrifyingly racist revision of the Path of Harmony is a prime example of the kind of nonsense that Revised Edition is infamous for?<br /> <br /> That would <i>also</i> be a tiresome argument, but at least it would be a more accurate view of this particular development within the gameline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","user":"Elphilm","date":". 02-23-2022, 05:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T05:21:03-08:00","id":1475307,"title":"","content":"The only reason the path fell out of practice was that the sabbat became way too violent. It would no doubt see some favor in sects like the Cam or the Anarchs where they follow humanity but tend to do things that goes against that to survive, like the jyhad and just rebelling against others tends to cause a lot of property damage. I feel that clans like the brujah, nosferatu, and gangrel would really appreciate this path, maybe even the odd gargoyle or two.<br /> <br /> Not saying its the best path, just that it gives a vampire a lot more freedom.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 02-23-2022, 08:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T05:46:30-08:00","id":1475309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475304#post1475304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not that anyone here will care, I suppose, but the above excerpt is what the actual Second Edition text says about the history and development of the Path of Harmony (emphases mine, of course). &quot;Native American beliefs&quot; are not mentioned even once in the writeup, nor are Harmonists identified with Native Americans anywhere in <i>The Players Guide to the Sabbat.</i><br /> <br /> The entire Path of Harmony = Native Americans thing seems to be a product of the Revised Edition version of the Path of Harmony in the <i>Sins of the Blood</i> supplement (pages 35-37). The Revised version is also responsible for the Path's &quot;protect the environment&quot; angle that is absent from the original.<br /> <br /> This has to be one of the most hilarious self-owns by Revised proponents I have ever seen on these forums. Should we qualify the assertions earlier in this thread by stating instead that this horrifyingly racist revision of the Path of Harmony is a prime example of the kind of nonsense that Revised Edition is infamous for?<br /> <br /> That would <i>also</i> be a tiresome argument, but at least it would be a more accurate view of this particular development within the gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, it seems more the &quot;Path of Angsty Gothic Romantics&quot;, put this way! I wonder why it was retconned in such a way (perhaps, to better bridge it towards the Path of the Beast). It's also paradoxical that the focus on protecting the environment as something &quot;un-Sabbat&quot; was done in Revised, considering that 2nd Edition strongly emphasized the alliance between Sabbat and Pentex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T07:07:00-08:00","id":1475317,"title":"","content":"Why is saying it was developed by indigenous Americans racist? It's not like it's saying that all indigenous people are Harmonists. Let me put it this way: I am, as the name might clue you in, mostly Cajun. Most Cajuns are Catholics. Not all of us. I'm an Atheist, but it is, by a wide margin, our most common religion. If I had read that some Cajun Sabbat had constructed a Path that heavily incorporated Catholic beliefs, I wouldn't be offended. If they said that every last Cajun member of the Sabbat was on that Path, THEN I would be offended. But a group of Cajuns constructing a Catholic oriented Path makes perfect sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T08:43:52-08:00","id":1475323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475249#post1475249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's work, but work the Sabbat regularly manages. So I'm pretty sure the Camarilla could have the necessary infrastructure to guide vampires bad at Humanity onto approved Paths.<br /> <br /> Esp. if you're running an altered version of the setting that better incorporates later additions like Roads into the history of the Camarilla and the Road of Kings and the Road of Heaven always had some presence in the Cam leading to modern Cam friendly versions of Paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for the fact the majority of Sabbat members before v5 were just low humanity instead of being on a path. In fact, majority of Sabbat don't survive the first month, unlike the Cam and Anarchs who on average survive a year. This coupled with the fact that a strong will is required to even get on a path means that the Sabbat only put 1 neonate on a path for every 50 that die. In other words, Sabbat don't &quot;managed&quot; as much as they throw neonates to die and see who survives.<br /> <br /> If Camarilla started encouraging neonates to practice a path, there would be a massive political backlash due to how the Sabbat already act. There would be a rift within the sect, and it would eat itself from the inside out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T10:19:27-08:00","id":1475332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475317#post1475317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is saying it was developed by indigenous Americans racist?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not the poster who made the argument originally, but I should probably clarify my own position in case my tongue in cheek post above should give the wrong impression: I don't think the original Second Edition writeup of the Path of Harmony, sans Native Americans, is particularly racist, nor do I find the Revised version that makes some allusions to indigenous Americans in the text particularly racist. I was only making fun of the idea that this Path of Harmony business is yet another example of the enlightened Revised Edition descending from the heavens to fix the mistakes of the &quot;horrifyingly racist&quot; Second Edition, when the real sequence of events is basically the opposite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T11:35:06-08:00","id":1475339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475304#post1475304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that anyone here will care, I suppose, but the above excerpt is what the actual Second Edition text says about the history and development of the Path of Harmony (emphases mine, of course). &quot;Native American beliefs&quot; are not mentioned even once in the writeup, nor are Harmonists identified with Native Americans anywhere in <i>The Players Guide to the Sabbat.</i><br /> <br /> The entire Path of Harmony = Native Americans thing seems to be a product of the Revised Edition version of the Path of Harmony in the <i>Sins of the Blood</i> supplement (pages 35-37). The Revised version is also responsible for the Path's &quot;protect the environment&quot; angle that is absent from the original.<br /> <br /> This has to be one of the most hilarious self-owns by Revised proponents I have ever seen on these forums. Should we qualify the assertions earlier in this thread by stating instead that this horrifyingly racist revision of the Path of Harmony is a prime example of the kind of nonsense that Revised Edition is infamous for?<br /> <br /> That would <i>also</i> be a tiresome argument, but at least it would be a more accurate view of this particular development within the gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for looking the original sourcebook. It's easy to forget details. And it caused me to look again to see if my own memory was wrong, or was using Revised era wording.<br /> <br /> There still seems to be a connection between the Path of Harmony and Native Americans, but it's a bit hidden. Throughout the Players Guide to the Sabbat, we're told that many Native Americans are part of the Country Gangrel and in fact make up most of the Country Gangrel recruits, and even those that aren't share &quot;certain&quot; Native American beliefs. And then in the Gangrel antitribu section, we're told that almost all Gangrel follow either the Path of Harmony or Honorable Accord. So this is where the connection is made.<br /> <br /> Other clans mentioned as following the Path of Harmony include &quot;some Brujah&quot;, that Harmony along with Honorable Accord and Caine are &quot;common&quot; among Nosferatu, &quot;a few Panders&quot;, &quot;most Ravnos antitribu&quot;, and &quot;a few&quot; Toreador.<br /> <br /> So overall we can say that the followers of the Path of Harmony are mostly within the Gangrel antitribu, Nosferatu antitribu, and Ravnos antitribu with only a few others elsewhere. This is probably a good indication this is a Path mainly followed by Nomad packs operating mostly in the wilderness, and not urban-based covens. It makes sense that the Path originated among Native Americans embraced by European &quot;country Gangrel&quot; in the early days and then spread elsewhere to other Nomad pack types. But that is interpretation, not explicit information.<br /> <br /> We're also told that one of the allies of the Sabbat are a few small groups of Native American shaman societies who provide safe havens and information in exchange from protection by Gangrel antitribu who also participate in mystic rites and offer advice. These have to be vampires who were Native Americans prior to their embrace. It doesn't make sense that they are from another race or culture. It makes the most sense these are Country Gangrel on the Path of Harmony who were Native Americans prior to their embrace and retain some connection to their old religion. This doesn't sound like Gangrel who would be on the Path of Honorable Accord which is heavily based on the Code of Milan (who by default are most likely to be City Gangrel who were driven out of the wilderness by the Country Gangrel - since we're told). <br /> <br /> It's not clear if these shaman societies realize they are dealing with vampires, or if they think they are some other kind of supernatural creature. But we are told the Native American Gangrel take refuge on the land of their own people. We are given the names of three of these societies, one of which is later described in the Book of Chantries in the Mage line.<br /> <br /> You're right that the description of the Path doesn't mention anything about Native Americans. But when combined with other information in the same Players Guide, I think the connection is solid.<br /> <br /> As written, all the talk of &quot;harmony&quot;, &quot;strong consciences&quot;, &quot;most humane&quot;, and living with nature roughly matches how many white Americans thought about Native Americans at the time as a result of the movie Dances with Wolves which was HUGELY influential in how Americans began to think about Native Americans in the nineties. It became the new stereotype. I would guess it was an attempt to make a humane path along the lines of Humanity but &quot;more appropriate&quot; for how they imagined cultural differences between European settlers/modern society and traditional Indian cultures.<br /> <br /> It also means that the Country Gangrel aren't your typical Sabbat and likely have few dealings with it. They're most likely Loyalists who are part of the Sabbat simply because it was the Sabbat who arrived in North America first when that sect was very different from the one described in the modern nights - one more about Sabbat freedom from the tyranny of the elders than a monstrous bunch of inhuman vampires under the control of a centralized hierarchy. Freedom, in this case, being &quot;leave us alone with out own people, we don't care what the rest of us do, but if the Camarilla vampires attack our people, we'll help out the other Sabbat.&quot; My interpretation of the facts.<br /> <br /> Obviously since the Path is also held a lot by Nosferatu and Ravnos antitribu, it has a following beyond that. And these variants of the Path are probably more universal and generic, while the Country Gangrel utilize more specific references of their own people. So it isn't solely based on Native American belief. It is just open to including those beliefs because that was likely the need of the original followers.<br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, the information found here means we have to translate &quot;the Sabbat purged the Path of Harmony&quot; to mean the Sabbat slaughtered almost the entirety of the Country Gangrel and the Ravnos antitribu, and a third of the Nosferatu antitribu. There is no way the Bishops could have done this without provoking a Fourth Sabbat Civil War. I just don't see the other Nosferatu antitribu turning against their kin, or the other Loyalists and Nomad packs agreeing to do this or tolerating it. In any case, it wouldn't have been easy or quick to do. So the offhand comment in Revised Sabbat that they were purged simply isn't compatible with early information. Once again, we're in an Earth-One and Earth-Two scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T12:00:05-08:00","id":1475341,"title":"","content":"It says that &quot;The Harmonists felt that the Sabbat's methods and ultimate ends were too destructive, both to the world and to individual members of the sect. The Path split. Some members embraced their bestial sides and rediscovered the far older <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Path_of_the_Feral_Heart\" target=\"_blank\">Path of the Feral Heart</a>. Most of the remaining &quot;true&quot; Harmonists perished, left the Sabbat, or learned to reconcile their faith with their sect loyalty (usually as nomads).&quot;<br /> <br /> I take that to mean that the only Harmonists who were actually purged were those who were too noisy about things like the Pentex alliance and other acts of mass destruction. Some Harmonists, especially nomads, just kept their mouths shut because the behavior of the Sabbat as a whole didn't affect them much. Some embraced or at least paid lip-service to converting to Feral Hearters. And some just straight-out left the Sabbat, which in the case of nomadic packs would barely be noticeable.<br /> <br /> The few Harmonists who actually got snuffed were likely high ranking members of founded covens who wouldn't shut the hell up about not damaging the environment. A &quot;Purge&quot; makes it sound like a mass slaughter, when the reality was likely just Cardinal Bob and Archbishop Jane and a few others who just could not seem to read the room when it came to their hippy environmentalist preaching.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T12:14:26-08:00","id":1475344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475323#post1475323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except for the fact the majority of Sabbat members before v5 were just low humanity instead of being on a path.</div> </div> </div> </div>And? The Sabbat still manages to get a significant number of its members onto Paths anyway.<br /> <br /> And something that seems forgotten: the Sabbat does curated and planned Embraces, not just mass Embraces and keep the survivors. The Cainites picked specifically for Embrace in the Sabbat tend to rise to power faster, and tend to have the mentor(s) necessary to get on a Path as safely as possible; most of them were chosen with that in mind in the first place.<br /> <br /> I'm not talking about the entire Cam switching to a Path like the OP was. I'm talking about the Cam being more open to a minority of its membership being on Paths that meet with Cam approval; as the advantages of that approach clearly outweigh the negatives.<br /> <br /> Also all of the Independent vampires that have Paths as a common trait in their membership that aren't the Sabbat meat grinder further reinforces that it is not, in fact, beyond the Cam's reach to have Paths as something some of their members do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Camarilla started encouraging neonates to practice a path, there would be a massive political backlash due to how the Sabbat already act. There would be a rift within the sect, and it would eat itself from the inside out. </div> </div> </div>So, you're quoting things and just ignoring what's actually in the quote then?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T12:34:46-08:00","id":1475346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475339#post1475339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, the information found here means we have to translate &quot;the Sabbat purged the Path of Harmony&quot; to mean the Sabbat slaughtered almost the entirety of the Country Gangrel and the Ravnos antitribu, and a third of the Nosferatu antitribu. There is no way the Bishops could have done this without provoking a Fourth Sabbat Civil War. I just don't see the other Nosferatu antitribu turning against their kin, or the other Loyalists and Nomad packs agreeing to do this or tolerating it. In any case, it wouldn't have been easy or quick to do. So the offhand comment in Revised Sabbat that they were purged simply isn't compatible with early information. Once again, we're in an Earth-One and Earth-Two scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to agree, but then again I think that most edition changes inevitably do violence to setting material. This doesn't apply only to <i>Vampire</i> or to White Wolf games in general, either. The Forgotten Realms has suffered through some astonishing bullshit with basically every single new edition of D&amp;D. Nowadays I think that the illusion of continuity that some fanbases try to maintain is a fool's errand. It would be so much less painful for everyone concerned if more people thought like you and considered each edition an alternate Earth instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T13:14:37-08:00","id":1475350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475341#post1475341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It says that &quot;The Harmonists felt that the Sabbat's methods and ultimate ends were too destructive, both to the world and to individual members of the sect. The Path split. Some members embraced their bestial sides and rediscovered the far older <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Path_of_the_Feral_Heart\" target=\"_blank\">Path of the Feral Heart</a>. Most of the remaining &quot;true&quot; Harmonists perished, left the Sabbat, or learned to reconcile their faith with their sect loyalty (usually as nomads).&quot;<br /> <br /> I take that to mean that the only Harmonists who were actually purged were those who were too noisy about things like the Pentex alliance and other acts of mass destruction. Some Harmonists, especially nomads, just kept their mouths shut because the behavior of the Sabbat as a whole didn't affect them much. Some embraced or at least paid lip-service to converting to Feral Hearters. And some just straight-out left the Sabbat, which in the case of nomadic packs would barely be noticeable.<br /> <br /> The few Harmonists who actually got snuffed were likely high ranking members of founded covens who wouldn't shut the hell up about not damaging the environment. A &quot;Purge&quot; makes it sound like a mass slaughter, when the reality was likely just Cardinal Bob and Archbishop Jane and a few others who just could not seem to read the room when it came to their hippy environmentalist preaching.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wouldn't Harmony 6 and 10 keep most harmonists from speaking openly to a group of murderous vampires on how they should not disturb the natural world. Also the harmonists who left the sabbat, wouldn't they be interested in seeing the path spread among the cam and anarchs. Sure some elders wont like that, but what are they going to do to a gangrel that can turn into mist and earth meld in somewhere with dirt? How would they even find them? It not like every tremere knows the ritual for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T13:25:36-08:00","id":1475351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475344#post1475344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, you're quoting things and just ignoring what's actually in the quote then?</div> </div> </div> </div>I only can make comments of things based off RAW and the like. If you want to remake the Cam to work with roads, which off meta is more recent then paths, then it would be an interesting idea. What I was trying to say, which I suppose wasn't communicated clearly, was that IF the cam did start having neonate members with paths, the ideological differences would cause in-fighting. Just look at the Sabbat, they've had multiple civil wars, and many can claim they're caused by the massive difference between path ideas specifically.<br /> <br /> While it's not beyond the possibility, I am saying it would be an interesting, though significant change that would require a damn good rewrite of the Camarilla in places. Unless you're going for a localized city trying this practice, which is more reasonable though likely to defect from the Cam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":26764,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","user":"Vilenecromancer","date":". 02-23-2022, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T14:40:15-08:00","id":1475360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475351#post1475351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I only can make comments of things based off RAW and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which includes the fact that the Cam has always had Path vampires in it, it's just currently a dirty secret sort of thing, rather than something openly acknowledged and used in order to minimize the disconnect from the meta. The early writing for the Cam has them opposed to Paths because Paths are a Sabbat thing. As the game expanded to Paths having formerly been common as Roads, and Path existing all over the place, the writing shifted to the Cam having Path vampires; just a small hidden minority that has to stay in the closet about it even if their Path is one of the tolerated ones.<br /> <br /> Since the setting-as-written-currently already has Cam vampires on Paths, the idea of some major conflict arising because it moves from a secret everybody knows but nobody talks about to a recognized and tolerated practice for <b>some</b> Paths, needs a lot more justification to it than you've provided. Since nobody is talking about every fresh neonate being encouraged to try out any Path they want, a bit more nuance would be appropriate in constructing an argument that moving to an more openly tolerant position would be meaningfully disruptive. It's not like purely Humanity vampires never have ideological struggles, and the Cam's Humanity only public position results in a kindred society without in-fighting. Many of the Paths that would make sense for the Cam to acknowledge (and to never have really lost) would inherently decrease in-fighting because in-fighting is something those Paths don't like (one of the better reasons for the Cam leadership to acknowledge those Paths, and create structures that influence otherwise troublesome vampires to join them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T14:46:18-08:00","id":1475361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475350#post1475350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wouldn't Harmony 6 and 10 keep most harmonists from speaking openly to a group of murderous vampires on how they should not disturb the natural world. Also the harmonists who left the sabbat, wouldn't they be interested in seeing the path spread among the cam and anarchs. Sure some elders wont like that, but what are they going to do to a gangrel that can turn into mist and earth meld in somewhere with dirt? How would they even find them? It not like every tremere knows the ritual for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably lower sins override higher sins, just as someone on Humanity can commit robbery to prevent someone being tortured to death.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T14:59:32-08:00","id":1475363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475361#post1475361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Presumably lower sins override higher sins, just as someone on Humanity can commit robbery to prevent someone being tortured to death.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_article-table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Not respecting a stronger vampire's <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Domain_(VTM)\" target=\"_blank\">domain</a>.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Predators do not seek danger.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Allowing gross disruption of the natural world.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">All things disrupt the world, simply by interacting with it. However, doing so deliberately is an attack on all things within the world.</td> </tr> </table></div> I feel like killing a couple humans isn't a gross disruption, now if were talking about burning down forests or throwing fireballs in the middle of the street, than yeah you're going to have to step in. But it never gets to that point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T15:22:44-08:00","id":1475366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475246#post1475246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would also be a lot of work. Keep in mind, you're not just teaching someone honor, you're pounding it into them so hard that it replaces humanity. </div> </div> </div> </div>That's called 'boot camp' and militaries do it to real life humans every single day... no vampirism needed.<br /> <br /> It wasn't always this way, but during WW2 it was noted that fewer than 10% of the infantry would even try to shoot an enemy even when their own life was in danger (while meanwhile noting that 90% of the soldiers would risk their lives to save a fellow soldier without a second thought). So our military set about a series of studies and programs designed to determine the best ways to essentially remove that hesitancy to murder another human being and by the start of the Gulf War had gotten that 10% number up to 99+%.<br /> <br /> Of course getting them deprogrammed afterwards has been problematic... the government breaks them and then doesn't much care about whether they're successfully able to re-integrate into civilian life.<br /> <br /> I've had a number of ex-military players in my games and all of them agreed that the Path of Honorable Accord better aligned with their personal codes of ethics than Humanity does. In my own games I put most military troops on Honorable Accord because otherwise their Humanity scores would need to be down about 3 to do what their orders often require them to do without remorse. Mechanically, humanity that low would also limit their Courage dice pools... whereas a solid Honorable Accord means they can be a fearless stone-cold sniper whose morality sees splattering an unsuspecting target's brains across a wall from 2000 yards as not only &quot;not wrong&quot;, but an unmitigated good if that's what their orders called for.<br /> <br /> In purely game terms I'd rank Path of Honorable Accord is one of the easier paths to switch too from Humanity because it still uses all the same virtues. You don't have to erode Conscience or Self-Control in order to adopt alien virtues, just switch their focus... a strong conscience and self-control are as good for Honorable Accord as they are for Humanity. The only danger is the flip itself, but even then I'd personally rule that you don't need to be especially low on the Humanity scale before you can adopt Honorable Accord... just low enough that killing for a cause is no longer an issue... about Humanity 3-4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T15:58:11-08:00","id":1475369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475168-why-don-t-more-vampires-follow-the-path-of-harmony-instead-of-humanity?p=1475366#post1475366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's called 'boot camp' and militaries do it to real life humans every single day... no vampirism needed.<br /> <br /> It wasn't always this way, but during WW2 it was noted that fewer than 10% of the infantry would even try to shoot an enemy even when their own life was in danger (while meanwhile noting that 90% of the soldiers would risk their lives to save a fellow soldier without a second thought). So our military set about a series of studies and programs designed to determine the best ways to essentially remove that hesitancy to murder another human being and by the start of the Gulf War had gotten that 10% number up to 99+%.<br /> <br /> Of course getting them deprogrammed afterwards has been problematic... the government breaks them and then doesn't much care about whether they're successfully able to re-integrate into civilian life.<br /> <br /> I've had a number of ex-military players in my games and all of them agreed that the Path of Honorable Accord better aligned with their personal codes of ethics than Humanity does. In my own games I put most military troops on Honorable Accord because otherwise their Humanity scores would need to be down about 3 to do what their orders often require them to do without remorse. Mechanically, humanity that low would also limit their Courage dice pools... whereas a solid Honorable Accord means they can be a fearless stone-cold sniper whose morality sees splattering an unsuspecting target's brains across a wall from 2000 yards as not only &quot;not wrong&quot;, but an unmitigated good if that's what their orders called for.<br /> <br /> In purely game terms I'd rank Path of Honorable Accord is one of the easier paths to switch too from Humanity because it still uses all the same virtues. You don't have to erode Conscience or Self-Control in order to adopt alien virtues, just switch their focus... a strong conscience and self-control are as good for Honorable Accord as they are for Humanity. The only danger is the flip itself, but even then I'd personally rule that you don't need to be especially low on the Humanity scale before you can adopt Honorable Accord... just low enough that killing for a cause is no longer an issue... about Humanity 3-4.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well here we get into the difference between the real world and the game system. In the real world, humans are tribalistic creatures who inherently feel empathy for their family the strongest, then increasingly small amounts of empathy the further away from their family people and creatures get, until you reach the point of, for example, fish, whom most of us can see staring back at us with dead eyes in the supermarket and feel utter sociopathic indifference towards. It doesn't really take all THAT much effort to get us to view, say, the military as our family, and enemy soldiers as being almost as much The Other to us as fish. We're not in danger of becoming wights. At most, we're in danger of viewing random civilians as The Other, and even that is the exception, not the rule. Our tribalism is malleable in a way that is rather, well, banal.<br /> <br /> Humanity, at least the old 10 sins hierarchy Humanity, isn't really something humans have inherently. Instead our variable empathy creates a vague, biased concept of fairness and we create laws based around that vague, heavily biased notion of fairness.<br /> <br /> Humanity is therefore a very artificial game construct based around the views of ethical philosophers and political theorists. The more you act in accordance with the views of ethical philosophers, the more &quot;human&quot; you are.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure you can really reconcile the reality of homo sapiens with game mechanics.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}